diff --git a/doc/board/apple/neo.rst b/doc/board/apple/neo.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..07205c1bc2becc6afed3800795ae69008bd278d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/board/apple/neo.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+MacBook Neo (T8140)
+==================
+
+This port uses the existing Apple NVMe, power-domain, pinctrl, mailbox and
+simple-framebuffer drivers. T8140 uses the existing M4-family CPU memory map.
+There is no native DCP firmware driver in U-Boot: m1n1 supplies an initialized
+framebuffer. U-Boot can display its console without renegotiating a display
+link or owning DCP firmware. Mode changes and new display connections remain
+the operating system's responsibility.
+
+Building
+--------
+
+The ``neo-bringup`` branch includes the existing Gravity Apple/NVMe changes
+from ``gravity-alpha-20260925`` and the Neo changes described here. With an
+AArch64 cross compiler installed, build from a fresh checkout on Linux::
+
+    make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- apple_m1_defconfig
+    make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- -j$(nproc) u-boot.bin
+
+On macOS, use GNU Make (``gmake``) and an appropriate AArch64 cross-compiler
+prefix. Standard U-Boot host prerequisites include a compiler, Python 3,
+Bison, Flex, OpenSSL development headers and ``dtc``. This Apple defconfig
+also builds EFI capsule tooling and needs the host GnuTLS development
+package (``libgnutls28-dev`` on Debian/Ubuntu).
+The tested payload is ``u-boot.bin``. It is a U-Boot payload, not a
+standalone Apple boot object. The tested stage 2 concatenates a raw m1n1
+image, the matching ``t8140-j700.dtb``, and gzip-compressed ``u-boot.bin``.
+Use a matching Neo m1n1 handoff implementation: it supplies the initialized
+framebuffer, firmware reservations, calibration and USB tuning metadata.
+
+USB
+---
+
+The T8130-generation ATC driver implements the shared USB2 host path used by
+both connectors. It initializes the dummy PIPE backend, separate PIPE clocks,
+USB2 power and host signals before releasing DWC3 reset. Host selection must
+be programmed while the PHY is off. The DWC3 driver consumes the factory host,
+cfg-host and PIPE tables exported from the live ADT by m1n1; do not substitute
+fixed tables from another machine. All register windows are DT named resources.
+
+The suspend-clock scale fallback and CIO timings match the already-tested
+Linux driver. Shutdown stops xHCI DMA before powering down the PHY, and OS
+handoff invokes shutdown even when the boot source is NVMe.
+
+Only USB2 is implemented by this initial PHY port. The SuperSpeed backend stays
+on dummy; this is not a USB3 or native DisplayPort implementation. SN201202x
+Type-C policy, negotiated orientation and the complete SuperSpeed PHY sequence
+are not ported. A native SuperSpeed port also needs a defined takeover of
+firmware-owned PHY/display state; the simple-framebuffer path does not own
+that firmware interface. Do not force a lane orientation or monitor-specific
+values.
+
+Validation: cross-build, repeated hardware starts enumerating the internal VIA
+USB2 hub, two successive start/stop cycles, and Linux subsequently mounting
+the on-disk ext4 root with all six CPUs online. That handoff test disabled the
+Linux USB/Type-C nodes, so it does not qualify Linux takeover of these devices.
+No external device was present in that test
+on the USB2-only connector (confirmed by SN201202x connection status).
+External mass-storage, external HID, both-connector hotplug and
+SuperSpeed have not been qualified. The USB3-capable connector is occupied
+by the development host during these tests.
+
+Subsequent automatic stage-1 -> stage-2 -> U-Boot -> Linux qualification
+passed twice with Linux USB/Type-C enabled, all six CPUs and an ext4 NVMe
+root. Linux bound both SN201202x controllers, enumerated the attached
+28.9 GiB USB drive, and read 4 MiB from it on each run. Saved kernel logs
+contained no Oops, warning, panic or SError. These runs use Linux callback
+fixes 93cae3f584a6 and 8527bd8a2146 on integration base a0126e397483.
+This verifies connected-device takeover; external U-Boot storage/HID and
+both-port hotplug remain unqualified.
+
+MTP
+---
+
+The Neo's keyboard/trackpad firmware uses a 2 MiB DMA receive ring; the
+existing U-Boot MTP driver understands only the older FIFO transport. The
+Neo is rejected during of_to_plat, before driver-model IOMMU attachment can
+replace the firmware mappings. Other machines retain the existing driver.
+
+The Linux driver documents ring registration and interface initialization,
+but does not provide a bootloader-to-Linux ring-unregister/cold-restart
+protocol. Existing U-Boot shutdown quiesces the helper and replays FIFO init
+messages; that is insufficient to establish the shared ring's lifetime.
+Also, probing the existing U-Boot DART driver replaces all firmware stream
+mappings. Keyboard bring-up would require resolving both issues first.
+
+MTP input is deliberately deferred under the instruction to skip features
+requiring additional reverse engineering of shutdown or OS handoff. No
+ring is registered, no speculative helper reset is attempted, and the
+firmware's mappings are left available for Linux. A USB keyboard can serve
+as boot input once external HID has been hardware-qualified.
+
+Provenance
+----------
+
+The register sequences and transport requirements above come from the
+existing Gravity Linux drivers at a0126e397483 and m1n1's ADT metadata.
+No Apple executable inspection or disassembly was used for this port.
diff --git a/drivers/input/apple_mtp_kbd.c b/drivers/input/apple_mtp_kbd.c
index e80e9a01c6f3596579429d09cb56a5a50765a493..51d94e8f768a070990560bd3e3419ac5f0f601c2 100644
--- a/drivers/input/apple_mtp_kbd.c
+++ b/drivers/input/apple_mtp_kbd.c
@@ -152,6 +152,19 @@ static int get_rtkit_helper(struct udevice *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Refuse unsupported ring firmware before DM probes its IOMMU. The FIFO
+ * handoff below cannot unregister a Neo shared-memory ring, and replacing
+ * the helper's firmware mappings would break the following Linux boot.
+ */
+static int apple_mtp_kbd_of_to_plat(struct udevice *dev)
+{
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "apple,t8140-dockchannel-hid")) {
+		dev_warn(dev, "Neo MTP ring handoff is not supported; preserving firmware state\n");
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int apple_mtp_kbd_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_mtp_kbd_priv *priv = dev_get_priv(dev);
@@ -240,6 +253,7 @@ U_BOOT_DRIVER(apple_mtp_kbd) = {
 	.name = "apple_mtp_kbd",
 	.id = UCLASS_KEYBOARD,
 	.of_match = apple_mtp_kbd_of_match,
+	.of_to_plat = apple_mtp_kbd_of_to_plat,
 	.probe = apple_mtp_kbd_probe,
 	.remove = apple_mtp_kbd_remove,
 	.priv_auto = sizeof(struct apple_mtp_kbd_priv),
